    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1271">

                <pb facs="1038" n="1028" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1028"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Ward, Angus I.: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-28T20:00:00+00:00">November 28,
                            1949—8 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 29—12:57 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4745. Substance Deptcirc November 23 and 26 re Ward case given Scarlett, Foreign
                    Office, this afternoon. Scarlett states British Pro-Consul, Mukden, had been
                    about to make representations Communists basis Deptcirc November 18 when on
                    learning of release of Ward had wired for further instructions. Foreign Office
                    will now direct Pro-Consul make comprehensive representations based in general
                    on information contained three Deptcircs mentioned herein. Scarlett agreed press
                    reports release Stokes did not alter seriousness case.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
